        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/de9cf531-5f49-4c90-b58a-83f755138c4a,1794594971868/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%28146%2C101%2C1639%2C921%29%3B' alt='An polar bear is captured on camera by a drone as part of a bear movement control experiment near Churchill, MB.' width='620' height='349' title='An adult polar bear stares up at the camera of a drone, the drone pilot is trying the scare the bear away from Churchill, MB.'/><p>While studies have shown drone hazing to be effective on black bears, researchers are now trying to see if it works with polar bears \u2014 a bigger, more curious and more aggressive species. The goal is to adapt the technology to Canada's North and try to take some of the risk out of managing the bears.</p>",
